  57:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * pcTail members are used as pointers into the queue storage area.  When the
  58:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * Queue_t structure is used to represent a mutex pcHead and pcTail pointers are
  59:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * not necessary, and the pcHead pointer is set to NULL to indicate that the
  60:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * structure instead holds a pointer to the mutex holder (if any).  Map alternative
  61:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * names to the pcHead and structure member to ensure the readability of the code
  62:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * is maintained.  The QueuePointers_t and SemaphoreData_t types are used to form
  63:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * a union as their usage is mutually exclusive dependent on what the queue is
  64:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c ****  * being used for. */
  65:../src/FreeRTOS/queue.c **** #define uxQueueType               pcHead
